  "description": "Classic aioli is made with nothing but garlic and olive oil pounded in a mortar and pestle. Our updated version uses egg yolks to help bind the sauce along with a hand blender to make it 100% foolproof and extremely quick.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: canola olive oil → vegetable olive oil or light olive oil\n\nNotes: Use the best quality extra virgin olive oil you can find but do not be tempted to add it directly to the hand blender cup—it will turn bitter. If you don't have an immersion blender with a cup, you can make the aioli in a food processor. Combine the egg, garlic, and lemon juice in a food processor. With the machine running, slowly drizzle in the canola or light olive oil, scraping down the sides as necessary. Transfer the half-finished aioli to a bowl and proceed with step two.",
